To create an interactive webpage that explains the correlation between carbon dioxide and global warming, you can start by outlining the key concepts and facts you want to convey. Then, use a combination of text, images, and interactive elements such as data visualization tools to present the information in an engaging and informative way. Some examples of interactive elements you could include are:
- Interactive graphs and charts that allow users to explore trends in carbon dioxide levels and temperature changes over time.
