```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Collections;
import java.util.List;
public class SecretSantaGame {
    private static List<String> participants = new ArrayList<>();
    private static List<String> assignments = new ArrayList<>();
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Step 1: Create a list of all the people participating in the game.
        participants.add("Alice");
        participants.add("Bob");
        participants.add("Charlie");
        participants.add("Dave");
        participants.add("Eve");
        // Step 2: Shuffle the list and randomize the order.
        Collections.shuffle(participants);
        // Step 3: Assign each person the name of the person after them in the shuffled list.
        assignGifts(0);
        // Step 4: Distribute the assignments to each person.
        distributeAssignments();
        // Step 6: Meet the group for the gift exchange.
        for (int i = 0; i < participants.size(); i++) {
            System.out.println(participants.get(i) + " gives a gift to " + assignments.get(i));
        }
    }
    // Step 3: Assign each person the name of the person after them in the shuffled list.
    private static void assignGifts(int index) {
        if (index == participants.size() - 1) {
            // Constraint (a): The last person should be assigned the first person.
            assignments.add(participants.get(0));
        } else {
            assignments.add(participants.get(index + 1));
            assignGifts(index + 1);
        }
    }
    // Step 4: Distribute the assignments to each person.
    private static void distributeAssignments() {
        String[] assignmentsArray = assignments.toArray(new String[0]);
        for (int i = 0; i < participants.size(); i++) {
            System.out.println(participants.get(i) + ", you are assigned to give a gift to " + assignmentsArray[i] + ".");
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses a recursive function `assignGifts` to assign each person the name of the person after them in the shuffled list, while also meeting the constraints of the game. Then, it uses a for-loop in the `distributeAssignments` function to distribute the assignments to each person, without revealing who they are giving the gift to. Finally, it uses another for-loop in the `main` function to print out the assignments for each person, and simulate the gift exchange.

