```
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
int main() {
   int arr[] = {3, 7, 1, 9, 5};
   int n = sizeof(arr)/sizeof(arr[0]);
   int max = arr[0];

   for(int i=1; i<n; i++) {
      if(arr[i] > max) {
         max = arr[i];
      }
   }

   cout << "The maximum element in the array is " << max << endl;
   return 0;
}
```
In this code, we first declare and initialize the array `arr`. We then calculate the size of the array using `sizeof(arr)/sizeof(arr[0])` and store it in the variable `n`. We then initialize the variable `max` to the first element of the array `arr[0]`.
We then loop through the array using a `for` loop starting from the second element of the array `arr[1]` till the last element of the array `arr[n-1]`. In each iteration of the loop, we compare the current element of the array with the maximum element `max`. If the current element is greater than `max`, we update the value of `max` to the current element.
Finally, we print the value of `max` which is the maximum element in the array.

