```
2. We define a function `read_csv` that takes a filename as input and returns a vector of vectors containing the data from the CSV file. This function reads the file line by line, splits each line into comma-separated values, converts each value from string to double, and adds the values to a vector of doubles representing a row. The row is then added to the data vector, which represents the entire CSV file. Finally, the function returns the data vector.
```cpp
vector<vector<double>> read_csv(string filename) {
    vector<vector<double>> data;
    ifstream file(filename);
    string line;
    while (getline(file, line)) {
        stringstream ss(line);
        vector<double> row;
        string value;
        while (getline(ss, value, ',')) {
            row.push_back(stod(value));
        }
        data.push_back(row);
    }
    file.close();
    return data;
}
```
3. We define four functions to calculate the mean, median, mode, and standard deviation of a vector of numbers. These functions are fairly straightforward and use basic mathematical operations to calculate the desired statistic. The `mean` function calculates the sum of the numbers and divides by the length of the vector. The `median` function first sorts the vector, then returns either the middle element (if the length of the vector is odd) or the average of the two middle elements (if the length of the vector is even). The `mode` function uses an unordered map to count the frequency of each number in the vector, then returns the number with the highest frequency. The `stdev` function first calculates the mean of the numbers, then calculates the sum of the squared differences between each number and the mean, divides by the length of the vector, and takes the square root of the result.
```cpp
double mean(vector<double> nums) {
    double sum = 0;
    for (double num : nums) {
        sum += num;
    }
    return sum / nums.size();
}
double median(vector<double> nums) {
    sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());
    int n = nums.size();
    if (n % 2 == 0) {
        return (nums[n/2 - 1] + nums[n/2]) / 2;
    } else {
        return nums[n/2];
    }
}
double mode(vector<double> nums) {
    unordered_map<double, int> freq;
    for (double num : nums) {
        freq[num]++;
    }
    int max_freq = 0;
    double mode = 0;
    for (auto pair : freq) {
        if (pair.second > max_freq) {
            max_freq = pair.second;
            mode = pair.first;
        }
    }
    return mode;
}
double stdev(vector<double> nums) {
    double avg = mean(nums);
    double sum = 0;
    for (double num : nums) {
        sum += pow(num - avg, 2);
    }
    return sqrt(sum / nums.size());
}
```
